# Keep the build context small and the image free of things it must not carry.
#
# data/ is the important line. It holds the 850 MB of DOL spreadsheets, their
# Parquet caches and the 63 MB SQLite database — none of which belong in a
# container that downloads its input from Blob. Without this line every image
# build ships the entire dataset twice over.

.git
.github
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo

data/
notebooks/
docs/
tests/
sql/
infra/

# NOT excluded, and this bit is load-bearing: app.py and .streamlit/ were
# listed here while Dockerfile.etl was the only image. Docker applies one
# .dockerignore to every build in the context, so leaving them would have made
# `COPY app.py .` in Dockerfile.web fail — or worse, silently ship the dashboard
# without its theme. The ETL image simply does not COPY them.

*.md
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile*
